Chapter: PunctualLaunderHead

 Probe (closed by the punctual FIX campaign): a call through a
 COMPUTED head - an if choosing between two non-punctual functions -
 is now rejected with CDX6001. Bounded execution requires every
 punctual call site to name its callee; indirect dispatch through a
 computed head is unbounded from the checker's seat, so the head
 shape itself is the error, before any callee question.

Section: Definitions

  slow-sum : Integer -> Integer
  slow-sum (n) = if n <= 0 then 0 else n + slow-sum (n - 1)

  slow-dbl : Integer -> Integer
  slow-dbl (n) = if n <= 0 then 0 else 2 + slow-dbl (n - 1)

  punctual spend : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  spend (c) (x) = (if c > 0 then slow-sum else slow-dbl) x

  opening : Text = show (spend 1 9)

